1
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:13,340
Let peace go lightly, and try drifting away.

2
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:26,880
Aiming for a certain day
floating on the Nakagawa River,

3
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:33,980
kick a pebble and even
your shoe goes flying.

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,240
And onto the head of the carpenter
whose savings I'd been keeping,

5
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:48,460
they laughed that I was still just a kid.

6
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:53,560
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:58,640
Katsushika, one more yawn,
and nothing changes.

8
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:02,500
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

9
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,480
From the pointed hat's water bottle,

10
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:16,780
the sun sets toward the great Tenmon.

11
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow, too, will end just like this.

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:29,080
Katsushika Shibamata,
they say that's happiness.

13
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:33,860
Running all over the place,
I finally realized, I'm such a fool.

14
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:41,640
Showdown! The golf course raid!

15
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:48,580
You're taking Ryotsu golfing?!

16
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:52,380
But he can't play golf at all, you know.

17
00:01:52,380 --> 00:01:53,540
That's exactly the point.

18
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:55,520
What do you mean by that?

19
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:58,620
Chief Kobashi from headquarters,
who's playing with us,

20
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:02,300
loves coaching so much he's known as
"Advice Kobashi."

21
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:05,720
I've heard that rumor.

22
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:08,180
He especially wants to coach beginners.

23
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:11,540
So someone who's a beginner has to join us.

24
00:02:12,140 --> 00:02:16,640
But Nakagawa owns several golf courses,

25
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:19,580
and Reiko plays at the
level of a women's pro.

26
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:24,200
My men have zero athletic ability,
so even with coaching they won't improve.

27
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:27,860
That leaves only Ryotsu, then.

28
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:31,260
Ryotsu's athletic ability alone
is better than most people's.

29
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:35,220
If he gets coaching and improves,
the chief will be pleased, that's the idea.

30
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:40,740
Anyway, on the day, be careful
not to show your true skill either.

31
00:02:41,740 --> 00:02:46,020
Though he's the one being coached,
frankly he's far worse than we are.

32
00:02:47,620 --> 00:02:50,140
Make sure you don't beat the chief,
even by mistake.

33
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:52,700
Be sure to tell Ryotsu the same, thoroughly.

34
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:53,920
Yes.

35
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:57,320
My stomach's already starting to hurt.

36
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:02,500
Wait, you agreed to play golf with a bigwig?

37
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:03,840
Is that right?

38
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,240
No way, Ryo-san.

39
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:07,440
There's no reason to refuse, is there?

40
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:10,120
Around the station,
Ryo-san is known for hating golf,

41
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:13,520
and people said he'd rather stick to
his own convictions than seek promotion.

42
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:15,580
They're sending a car to pick you up,

43
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:18,080
and they're even feeding you, too.

44
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:20,520
This is a chance to build up your strength,
isn't it?

45
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:21,860
But, senpai,

46
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:23,860
you've never played golf even once,
have you?

47
00:03:23,860 --> 00:03:25,640
Don't underestimate me.

48
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:30,180
The other day,
I got two holes-in-one on a par-72 course.

49
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:32,500
I played 24 under par.

50
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:33,700
24 under?

51
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:37,640
I've never heard of even a pro
golfer posting a score like that.

52
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:41,820
The Open at St Andrews
and the Masters at Augusta,

53
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:46,280
even those tough courses,
my best score was only 18 under.

54
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:49,060
When did you go to Britain and America?

55
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:53,320
I get it, Senpai.
You mean that video game, right?

56
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:56,040
Yeah, it's the software called "Our Golf."

57
00:03:56,600 --> 00:04:00,620
Geez, don't scare me like that.
Ryo-chan, you're just mixing up the game and

58
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:04,960
real golf is different.
Don't tell me that. I've got Tiger's power.

59
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:08,040
I've got power like hitting, like a pro.
Golf's a piece of cake.

60
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:11,220
More like gorilla power than Tiger's, right?

61
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:17,380
What, who are you calling a gorilla?
Anyway, Senpai, what about your clubs?

62
00:04:17,380 --> 00:04:22,160
What are you going to do? You don't have any,
right? Right, I'll borrow yours.

63
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:24,400
You've got plenty, haven't you?

64
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:25,420
Of course, that's fine.

65
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:27,260
Then I'll bring one tomorrow.

66
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:29,840
That won't do. Absolutely not!

67
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:32,400
Chief, good morning!

68
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:36,640
Chief, why can't I use my clubs?

69
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:39,420
How much is your whole golf set worth?

70
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:42,340
Well, they're all premium pieces, so...

71
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:44,700
Roughly ten million yen, I'd say.

72
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:46,140
Ten million yen?

73
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:48,200
That's exactly why it's not allowed.

74
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:52,000
Using clubs more expensive than the headquarters
chief's would be entirely out of the question.

75
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:56,657
I'll lend you the set I bought
15 years ago for 30,000 yen.

76
00:04:56,707 --> 00:04:57,520
Use that one.

77
00:04:58,180 --> 00:04:59,651
And like I said yesterday,

78
00:04:59,701 --> 00:05:03,380
Chief Kobashi loves to teach,
so just listen obediently, got it?

79
00:05:03,820 --> 00:05:06,284
Whatever you do, don't accidentally win.

80
00:05:06,334 --> 00:05:09,440
If you defy him, I'll have you
sent to the most remote police box.

81
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:14,178
Golf with bigwigs isn't
really about playing golf,

82
00:05:14,228 --> 00:05:16,800
it's 99% flattery, you know.

83
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:19,480
Ryo-chan,
you've really taken on something big.

84
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:21,580
Good thing it wasn't me.

85
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:34,380
Hey, how long are you
going to keep sleeping?

86
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:35,960
We're here.
Are you going to carry the luggage or what?

87
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:41,340
I haven't gotten up this early since
the elementary school field trip.

88
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:43,740
Why does golf always start
so early in the morning?

89
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:44,320
Alright!

90
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:51,420
Come on, pull yourself together, properly!

91
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:52,560
Yo-shi-kun.

92
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:55,640
Eeeeh! Good morning.

93
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:58,060
Here's Chief... Chief Kobashi, sir.

94
00:05:58,060 --> 00:06:07,460
Good morning. We've been waiting for you. I believe
the meeting time was set for seven o'clock, though.

95
00:06:08,020 --> 00:06:13,520
Well, knowing it's golf, I woke up early.
I got here at 3 in the morning.

96
00:06:14,740 --> 00:06:17,840
It's just like a school field trip when we were kids,
isn't it?

97
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:22,000
Hey, greet them properly! Greet them!

98
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:22,780
Hello.

99
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:24,720
This is my subordinate, Ryotsu.

100
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:28,560
Today is my first time playing golf,
so I'm counting on your guidance.

101
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:30,700
So it's your debut match

102
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,900
Don't be so stiff, just go for it.

103
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:35,300
I'll give you some advice,
so don't you worry.

104
00:06:36,900 --> 00:06:38,680
Please, I'm in your hands.

105
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:43,140
Alright then, every minute counts,
let's get started right away.

106
00:06:51,660 --> 00:06:52,860
Nice shot!

107
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:56,320
It didn't fly very far, though.

108
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:57,860
No, no, it's magnificent.

109
00:06:57,860 --> 00:06:59,840
It landed right in the
middle of the fairway.

110
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:01,780
A beautiful shot, flying straight.

111
00:07:01,780 --> 00:07:02,860
As expected of the Chief!

112
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:04,340
The ball's trajectory is so clean, I'd say.

113
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:05,960
Or rather, it's artistic.

114
00:07:06,380 --> 00:07:07,120
Do you think so?

115
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:10,480
For all the showing off you did,

116
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:11,520
it doesn't go very far, does it?

117
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:15,820
But still...

118
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:20,860
I know, I know.

119
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:28,820
Into the pond again. Yeah, I'm hopeless.

120
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:31,080
Your right shoulder is dropping too much.

121
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:33,560
And you have to watch the ball properly.

122
00:07:34,780 --> 00:07:39,200
I see, I see.
Well, the chief's advice is truly helpful.

123
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:45,000
Honestly, how can anyone lay on flattery
that makes your ass itch like that?

124
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:48,660
Hey, Ryotsu! What are you spacing out for?
It's your turn!

125
00:07:49,020 --> 00:07:49,620
Yes, yes.

126
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:53,340
Listen, Ryotsu, whatever you do,
play worse than the chief.

127
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:54,900
Don't you dare show off.

128
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:58,540
Yeah, yeah, I'm just a lowly box cop.
I know that.

129
00:08:00,140 --> 00:08:02,680
Finally, my first time golfing.
Let's do this!

130
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:06,060
No, that's where you're wrong.

131
00:08:06,980 --> 00:08:08,420
This is how you hold the grip.

132
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:09,540
Like this?

133
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:12,380
You're gripping too hard.
Swing more lightly.

134
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:13,880
Lightly, lightly, lightly.

135
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:21,960
That's it, Ryo-chan. Come on, twist your hips more and keep your left elbow straight.
Don't spread your feet out like that.

136
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:25,980
For your swing, picture building a wall on your left side.
A wall, got it?

137
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:28,980
Now practice your swing again right there.

138
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:33,960
A wall on the left side, right?
Heave-ho, heave-ho.

139
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:36,440
What are you doing?

140
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:41,300
I tried building a wall on my left side in my mind.
How was that?

141
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:43,360
That's not what I meant.

142
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:46,220
I told you to build up
power on your left side.

143
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:50,220
If that's what you meant,
you should have said it more clearly.

144
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:50,840
Uh-oh.

145
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:53,320
Hey Ryotsu,
that's rude to the headquarters chief!

146
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:57,700
No, the chief's advice is wonderful, but

147
00:08:57,700 --> 00:09:00,980
he's a simple-minded guy,
so he just can't understand it.

148
00:09:00,980 --> 00:09:01,920
Is that so?

149
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:03,560
Yeah, right.

150
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:06,980
Let's get this over with
and go home for a good meal.

151
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:08,620
Ready, go!

152
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:10,700
That's what I just said, didn't I?

153
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:14,860
Raise the club, pull back your hips,
and swing down in a circle.

154
00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:18,320
Shut up already, I get it.
Like this, like this, in a circle.

155
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:20,920
How's that?

156
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:27,760
It's not going anywhere at all!

157
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:31,220
You didn't do what I told you.

158
00:09:31,700 --> 00:09:34,320
Good, that's it, keep it up, Ryotsu!

159
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:39,320
I did exactly what the Chief taught me,
and it still won't fly at all!

160
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:43,020
Keep doing it just like that.

161
00:09:43,020 --> 00:09:43,960
Understood.

162
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:50,760
The trees are in the way if I want
to get it onto the green from here.

163
00:09:50,760 --> 00:09:53,860
Honestly, you keep giving me weird advice.

164
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:55,980
Now I've gone and hit
it into a spot like this!

165
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:58,580
Here, through the gap between those trees,

166
00:09:58,580 --> 00:10:01,900
You're not seriously thinking of squeezing it through the trees,
are you?

167
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:05,560
From the side here,
you need to get it safely onto the fairway.

168
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:07,260
No, but this much should be fine...

169
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:10,480
Damn it.

170
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:14,560
If the Chief's advice runs out,
my score's gonna get even worse.

171
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:18,300
But still, there's no choice
here but to go through the trees.

172
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:21,940
Isn't that Norika Fujiwara over there?

173
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,180
I've done it now!

174
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:29,440
Chief!

175
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:34,100
Ryotsu!

176
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:37,460
Well, I hit it just like you said,
but I'm not very good at this.

177
00:10:37,460 --> 00:10:41,560
Listen, do that again and you won't just be kept off the course,
you'll be fired!

178
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:42,060
Yes.

179
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:47,120
Now it's a bunker

180
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:50,260
Chief, how should I hit a shot like this?

181
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:52,140
Y-yeah, well...

182
00:10:52,140 --> 00:10:54,020
L-just watch me do it.

183
00:10:54,020 --> 00:10:55,880
Chief, we've been waiting for this!

184
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:57,860
I'd love to see a model demonstration.

185
00:10:57,860 --> 00:11:00,400
For this kind,
you have to set your footing firmly

186
00:11:04,100 --> 00:11:05,400
That last one was a bad example.

187
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:19,440
C-chief, this isn't looking good.

188
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:23,180
Now that I think about it, Chief Kobashi,
I forgot you're bad at bunkers.

189
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:26,380
W-what a disaster.

190
00:11:26,980 --> 00:11:30,200
Not like me at all,
but this time I'll hit it!

191
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:32,347
Now, now, Chief,

192
00:11:32,397 --> 00:11:35,440
you won't get anywhere with
your head full of blood.

193
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:37,060
Deep breaths, deep breaths.

194
00:11:37,460 --> 00:11:40,820
Shut up! You amateur,
do you really think you can give me advice?

195
00:11:42,005 --> 00:11:46,020
Chief! Don't mind what he says,
just play at your own pace!

196
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:49,480
Idiot! What the hell am I
supposed to say to this idiot?

197
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:56,440
Losing if my blood rises? How insolent...

198
00:11:58,950 --> 00:12:03,960
Nice shot! Just as expected of you, Chief!

199
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:12,220
I see, so basically I just have
to smack the sand as hard as I can

200
00:12:12,220 --> 00:12:13,080
Alright!

201
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:18,660
Count me in! Hey, this is easy!

202
00:12:21,420 --> 00:12:23,240
You're not half bad, are you?

203
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:26,100
It was a fluke, just a fluke. Pure luck.

204
00:12:27,780 --> 00:12:30,960
Yeah, I figure. It's beginner's luck.

205
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:36,800
Hey, hey, don't show off just
because you're a beginner.

206
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:38,100
Hurry up and hit it!

207
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:38,840
Yes, yes.

208
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:43,900
But this looks like the 8th green in our golf game,
doesn't it?

209
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:47,460
If you aim for that spot...

210
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:49,400
Yes! I've got it figured out!

211
00:12:49,820 --> 00:12:51,580
After that, it's just like the game.

212
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:54,580
Don't you dare compare it to a game!

213
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:56,500
That's fair enough.

214
00:12:56,920 --> 00:12:58,760
Sorry, but I'll take it.

215
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:02,820
Mm, there we go. Nice shot!

216
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:03,920
Big

217
00:13:06,580 --> 00:13:11,180
Ha well then, I got lucky! No way...

218
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:20,180
Ryotsu, after I told him so many times... I can't believe it. One long putt,
and a beginner, twice!

219
00:13:20,180 --> 00:13:28,400
Are you calling it beginner's luck? No, it's all thanks to the Chief's advice!
But you didn't give any putting advice, did you?

220
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:30,560
I don't feel well. I'm going in!

221
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:31,160
Aaah!

222
00:13:31,740 --> 00:13:34,980
Chief, please, not that, anything but that!

223
00:13:35,060 --> 00:13:37,604
You idiot! I told you so many times...

224
00:13:37,654 --> 00:13:39,240
You're fired, effective today!

225
00:13:39,540 --> 00:13:40,480
What? No way!

226
00:13:41,160 --> 00:13:41,760
This is terrible!

227
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:44,160
It's the Golg Castle raid!

228
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:46,700
Golg Castle raid?

229
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:48,240
Right!

230
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:50,240
That's right, I challenge you!

231
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:51,300
Hurry!

232
00:13:56,660 --> 00:14:00,140
If there's no pro who can beat us,
the Muramame Four Brothers,

233
00:14:00,140 --> 00:14:03,140
we're taking this golf
course's sign with us!

234
00:14:05,940 --> 00:14:09,420
The Muramame Four Brothers?
Who are these guys?

235
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:25,060
Get the manager out here, quick.

236
00:14:25,060 --> 00:14:25,420
Yes.

237
00:14:26,980 --> 00:14:28,620
These must be new extortionists.

238
00:14:28,620 --> 00:14:29,840
Watch yourselves.

239
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:30,500
Yes.

240
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:32,460
Speaking of which, Chief.

241
00:14:32,460 --> 00:14:35,140
I got fired from the police just now,
didn't I?

242
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:36,440
Bakabon.

243
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:38,340
Is now really the time for that?

244
00:14:38,340 --> 00:14:39,580
Just get going.

245
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:42,480
Honestly, you're so full of yourself.

246
00:14:43,140 --> 00:14:44,340
Hey, you lot.

247
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:47,360
We shouldn't be extorting people, now.

248
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:48,820
Who are you?

249
00:14:48,820 --> 00:14:50,220
We're with the police.

250
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:51,820
The police?

251
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:54,940
Good sir,
you seem to have some misunderstanding.

252
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:57,380
We haven't been extorting anyone!

253
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:59,800
That's right, we just want a match.

254
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:02,580
We never once said we wanted money!
Here, take it.

255
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:05,360
Well, thank you very much.

256
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:07,640
Are you the manager?

257
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:08,380
Y-yes.

258
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:10,800
Please, spare us the sign.

259
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,140
With this, please just take your leave.

260
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:15,920
That much?

261
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:18,760
What should we do, big brother?

262
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:21,400
We never actually said
we wanted money, did we?

263
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:25,240
If nobody's willing to take us on,
then it's fine to just accept it, isn't it?

264
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:28,360
Wait a minute!

265
00:15:28,860 --> 00:15:29,260
What?

266
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:31,340
I'll take you on myself.

267
00:15:31,340 --> 00:15:34,040
Are you saying you'll accept our challenge?

268
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:36,540
You plan to win with your dirty tricks,
I suppose.

269
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:38,460
Things won't go your way.

270
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:40,960
So this money is on hold for now.

271
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:42,680
Deal?

272
00:15:42,680 --> 00:15:46,080
But no one has ever beaten
us after challenging us.

273
00:15:46,680 --> 00:15:47,940
Bring it on.

274
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:49,800
Don't take us lightly.

275
00:15:50,980 --> 00:15:52,520
Now it's getting interesting.

276
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:55,060
By the way, about this money,

277
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:57,460
if we win, we get to keep it, right?

278
00:15:58,520 --> 00:16:00,820
Are you sure you're fine
with us taking the sign?

279
00:16:01,220 --> 00:16:03,800
N-no, no, y-yes, of course.

280
00:16:04,660 --> 00:16:07,700
Ryotsu, are you sure it's wise
to say something like that?

281
00:16:07,980 --> 00:16:09,820
When you can't even play golf properly.

282
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:11,940
It's fine.

283
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:16,000
Against that sort of riffraff, the best
thing is to hit them with a solid shot.

284
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:19,980
I'm glad I brought
stomach medicine after all.

285
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:21,120
Give me some too.

286
00:16:21,700 --> 00:16:23,780
The match rules: just one hole.

287
00:16:23,780 --> 00:16:25,840
No penalties like out-of-bounds.

288
00:16:25,840 --> 00:16:28,540
Either way, whoever uses fewer strokes wins.

289
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:30,700
Let's see what you've got, shall we?

290
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:32,860
Come at us from wherever you like,
we're ready for you!

291
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:36,200
First up, this humble one.

292
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:37,660
Nisaimon, the Spear.

293
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:47,280
Ooh!

294
00:16:47,280 --> 00:16:49,540
Hahaha! How about that? Did you see?

295
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:52,580
W-wow! That went 300 yards!

296
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:55,320
So these guys weren't just all talk!

297
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:57,820
Number two, focus like an iaido swordsman!

298
00:16:58,260 --> 00:16:58,780
Here I go!

299
00:17:00,980 --> 00:17:02,620
A No. 2 iron here, I think.

300
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:11,060
I can't see the swing.

301
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:13,180
Wow, this one's going far too!

302
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,340
Showing off like that.

303
00:17:19,340 --> 00:17:21,540
Just shoot normally, normally!

304
00:17:22,860 --> 00:17:25,640
Next, I, Chin-Ran-Ran, make my entrance!

305
00:17:25,640 --> 00:17:28,180
Why are you the only one who
looks like a Chinese magic troupe?

306
00:17:28,540 --> 00:17:30,940
Weren't we supposed to be the
Muramame Four Brothers, anyway?

307
00:17:30,940 --> 00:17:32,460
Why are you Chin-Ran?

308
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:33,820
Our surname is Muramame!

309
00:17:33,820 --> 00:17:35,560
Chin-Ran-Ran from China, that's me!

310
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:47,860
Amazing,
all three of them went over 300 yards!

311
00:17:48,380 --> 00:17:50,880
This is no opponent for Ryotsu to take on.

312
00:17:52,060 --> 00:17:52,940
Well, what do you know.

313
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:55,560
If it's that much power, I won't lose.

314
00:17:55,920 --> 00:17:58,480
I was holding back earlier,
out of respect for the Chief.

315
00:17:58,480 --> 00:18:00,200
This time I'm going all out.

316
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:01,040
What?

317
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:03,960
So you weren't serious until now?

318
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:06,001
No, I mean, well...

319
00:18:06,051 --> 00:18:08,840
He just has tremendous brute strength,
you see.

320
00:18:11,220 --> 00:18:12,820
Hey, don't be surprised when you see this!

321
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:14,200
Yaaaaah!

322
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:19,620
W-wow!

323
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:21,460
But his form is all over the place.

324
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:25,300
Y-yeah. No matter how far it goes,
with form like that...

325
00:18:25,540 --> 00:18:26,540
Right?

326
00:18:27,160 --> 00:18:29,960
Still, it flew 350 yards.

327
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:33,160
How about that! Take that, suckers!

328
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:36,600
Sasuke, understood!

329
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:50,392
My ball,

330
00:18:50,442 --> 00:18:52,900
I'm sure it came down around here.

331
00:18:53,380 --> 00:18:55,920
Looks like Sasuke pulled it off.

332
00:18:57,900 --> 00:19:00,320
Found it! Ryotsu, it's over there!

333
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:02,820
Why is it way over there?

334
00:19:02,820 --> 00:19:04,800
It should have stopped on the fairway.

335
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:07,320
It must have hit a rock and bounced off.

336
00:19:07,320 --> 00:19:08,620
Bad luck

337
00:19:08,620 --> 00:19:09,920
Are you going to give up?

338
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:11,840
Shut up! I'm not losing!

339
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:13,860
I'll get it through no matter what!

340
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:17,340
No good, Ryotsu.
We have to get it back to the fairway first.

341
00:19:17,900 --> 00:19:20,300
If you do that,
you'll lose a stroke, won't you?

342
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:24,620
Even so, there are trees in
the direction of the green,

343
00:19:26,340 --> 00:19:27,820
Just watch this.

344
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:34,600
Yes, it's heading in the right direction!

345
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:36,360
W-what are you planning to do?

346
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:38,540
There!

347
00:19:42,860 --> 00:19:44,520
How about that? That's two on the green!

348
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:46,980
What kind of trick is that?

349
00:19:46,980 --> 00:19:49,500
Ryo-tsu doesn't even know the rules well.

350
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:51,740
That shot is unorthodox, isn't it?

351
00:19:52,180 --> 00:19:53,640
No, it's wonderful.

352
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:56,200
His method is totally reckless, but

353
00:19:57,820 --> 00:19:59,460
his guts are impressive.

354
00:19:59,460 --> 00:20:01,340
As expected of the Chief!

355
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:03,880
We tell our juniors to at least learn

356
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:05,900
from his guts, too.

357
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:08,000
Hey, Nao-hara-kun.

358
00:20:09,460 --> 00:20:11,240
That's right, Chief.

359
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:13,640
Not bad at all.

360
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:15,800
But it's too early to celebrate.

361
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:17,920
Just watch.

362
00:20:18,460 --> 00:20:19,320
Rengetsu-dan!

363
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:21,100
Original Scatter Shot!

364
00:20:25,660 --> 00:20:26,460
Hey,

365
00:20:27,820 --> 00:20:28,820
It got knocked off the rim!

366
00:20:30,260 --> 00:20:30,900
Damn it!

367
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:32,377
Those guys,

368
00:20:32,427 --> 00:20:36,600
always going after my ball, the bastards!

369
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:40,900
And now, here comes the grand magic!

370
00:20:46,180 --> 00:20:48,760
No way!
I can't believe they pulled that off!

371
00:20:49,180 --> 00:20:52,320
What's wrong?
All three of us cleared it, didn't we?

372
00:20:52,620 --> 00:20:54,620
Where'd your ball go?

373
00:20:54,620 --> 00:20:57,480
Well? Are you going to admit defeat?

374
00:20:57,480 --> 00:21:02,360
Damn it! Take all our clubs!

375
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:05,980
What do you think you're doing?
It's pointless, no matter what you try.

376
00:21:05,980 --> 00:21:10,060
Pulling stunts like that only fires me up even more.
That's just my nature.

377
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:11,480
I'm going to win, no matter what!

378
00:21:12,460 --> 00:21:16,420
Done! If you're going short,
we'll go with super-long clubs!

379
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:24,560
Yes! We did it!

380
00:21:24,620 --> 00:21:27,320
Nice putt! Well done, Ryotsu!

381
00:21:27,940 --> 00:21:30,320
Damn, what a guy!

382
00:21:30,740 --> 00:21:34,220
Now, the putt. Since mine is the farthest away,
I'll go first.

383
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:37,420
Hey Ryotsu, this isn't billiards!

384
00:21:37,660 --> 00:21:40,000
A trick shot calls for
a trick shot in return.

385
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:42,700
Ryo-san Dahoo, reverse billiards!

386
00:21:46,300 --> 00:21:48,120
Right into the bunker I hate most!

387
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:50,660
It was dropped into the pond!

388
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:53,420
Aiya, it landed in the rough!

389
00:21:54,620 --> 00:21:55,080
Look!

390
00:21:55,240 --> 00:21:56,700
Look! It's going in the cup!

391
00:21:59,140 --> 00:21:59,980
No good!

392
00:21:59,980 --> 00:22:01,820
Don't worry! Sasuke's here!

393
00:22:03,040 --> 00:22:03,720
Stop!

394
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:13,040
Damn it!

395
00:22:13,420 --> 00:22:15,240
What is that guy doing over there?!

396
00:22:15,480 --> 00:22:18,680
So that's who made it so
Ryotsu-kun couldn't hit his ball!

397
00:22:18,820 --> 00:22:20,280
Yes, the rules…

398
00:22:22,220 --> 00:22:23,520
Alright, I'll go first!

399
00:22:23,520 --> 00:22:25,420
I holed it in four strokes!

400
00:22:25,820 --> 00:22:27,180
So, what now?

401
00:22:27,180 --> 00:22:28,520
Muramame Four Brothers

402
00:22:28,520 --> 00:22:29,900
Are you going to give up?

403
00:22:29,900 --> 00:22:33,120
Or do you still plan to
win with your dirty tricks?

404
00:22:33,700 --> 00:22:34,560
Well, we surrender.

405
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:36,520
We were completely defeated.

406
00:22:38,580 --> 00:22:39,640
Let this be a lesson

407
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:41,320
and never pull a stunt like this again.

408
00:22:41,320 --> 00:22:43,400
I'll let it slide this time.

409
00:22:43,780 --> 00:22:44,740
Now get lost!

410
00:22:47,300 --> 00:22:49,280
All talk and no game, these guys.

411
00:22:50,280 --> 00:22:52,000
Now that money is mine.

412
00:22:52,440 --> 00:22:53,260
Ryotsu-kun.

413
00:22:54,900 --> 00:22:56,720
No, that was a splendid play.

414
00:22:56,720 --> 00:22:57,920
Uh, th-thank you.

415
00:22:57,920 --> 00:22:59,780
It seems I misjudged you.

416
00:22:59,780 --> 00:23:03,060
I'd really like to play
together again sometime.

417
00:23:03,060 --> 00:23:06,460
I'm sorry, but I can't attend next time.

418
00:23:06,460 --> 00:23:09,400
Actually, I'm being fired as of today.

419
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:10,640
What are you talking about!

420
00:23:10,720 --> 00:23:12,280
You're a capable subordinate.

421
00:23:12,280 --> 00:23:13,880
Keep up the good work from now on.

422
00:23:15,020 --> 00:23:17,000
To have raised a fighter like him

423
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,260
A splendid piece of writing indeed.

424
00:23:18,260 --> 00:23:20,460
We should have others learn from him.

425
00:23:20,460 --> 00:23:22,460
I'm honored.

426
00:23:22,460 --> 00:23:24,880
Ryotsu is the pride of our station!

427
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:26,860
I don't know what's going on, but

428
00:23:26,860 --> 00:23:28,680
Looks like he escaped the collar.

429
00:23:31,100 --> 00:23:33,660
Thank you so much, that really helped.

430
00:23:33,660 --> 00:23:35,780
As promised, here it is.

431
00:23:35,780 --> 00:23:38,180
Idiot! Who brings that at a time like this?

432
00:23:39,480 --> 00:23:40,560
What's that?

433
00:23:41,080 --> 00:23:43,360
Don't tell me you did
all this just for money?

434
00:23:43,360 --> 00:23:47,600
N-no, of course not!

435
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:52,420
Ryotsu! You're fired, effective today!

436
00:23:53,020 --> 00:23:53,440
Whoa!

437
00:23:53,720 --> 00:23:54,440
Seriously!?

438
00:23:55,160 --> 00:23:59,220
No way! I hate golf now!

439
00:24:18,260 --> 00:24:27,340
If you're the one who's suffering,
waking up feels good

440
00:24:28,200 --> 00:24:31,760
Even the boring stories

441
00:24:31,760 --> 00:24:36,540
Set my whole body on fire

442
00:24:36,780 --> 00:24:43,200
But I want to see my friends

443
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:58,320
I want to be loved for sure, like we're melting together,
so much that everyone might be a little annoyed

444
00:24:58,940 --> 00:25:02,440
I definitely want to confide

445
00:25:02,960 --> 00:25:07,880
Somehow, only love is out of tune

446
00:25:08,700 --> 00:25:12,240
Even the bravado

447
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:15,800
Don't hide everything

448
00:25:20,840 --> 00:25:24,040
What? A visual-kei band member
is the temporary station chief?

449
00:25:24,260 --> 00:25:26,540
Charlie Kobayashi?
I've never even heard of him!

450
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:30,080
He must be a fake visual-kei fan, right?

451
00:25:30,440 --> 00:25:31,320
Wait a minute...

452
00:25:31,320 --> 00:25:33,500
I've seen that face somewhere before

453
00:25:33,940 --> 00:25:36,300
Next time: Charlie Kobayashi's secret

454
00:25:36,740 --> 00:25:37,320
Nice to meet you

